{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794564820665,"sessionID":"ses_e2b9b776cffe9oHJ15dLLxNWNn","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4660cdf001F74vlTYSahGKkQ","sessionID":"ses_e2b9b776cffe9oHJ15dLLxNWNn","messageID":"msg_1d465f662001Y2f0VtDmQogpYH","type":"tool","id":"call_5c9816030a724a1f85c0d01f","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md","limit":80},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md, lines 1-80\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Rule: Communication\"\n3: description: \"Write so the reader can act after one pass: no table in a reply, nothing that does not carry information.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"cut filler\"\n6:   - \"empty opener\"\n7:   - \"match length to the question\"\n8:   - \"no tables\"\n9:   - \"can you say that more plainly\"\n10:   - \"I don't follow\"\n11:   - \"too abstract\"\n12:   - \"number the steps\"\n13:   - \"item cap\"\n14:   - \"reply too long\"\n15:   - \"say each fact once\"\n16:   - \"one idea per sentence\"\n17:   - \"plain words\"\n18:   - \"em dash\"\n19:   - \"reads like terminal output\"\n20:   - \"concise is not compressed\"\n21:   - \"recommend one option\"\n22:   - \"buried the verdict\"\n23:   - \"say where you are going\"\n24:   - \"time estimate\"\n25: importance_tier: important\n26: contextType: reference\n27: version: 1.5.0.0\n28: ---\n29: \n30: # Rule: Communication\n31: \n32: > Routed from [`REPO RULES.md`](../../REPO%20RULES.md). Load before writing any substantive reply.\n33: > Expands `AGENTS.md`, never overrides it. Where they appear to disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins and this file is wrong. Say so.\n34: \n35: ## Fires when\n36: \n37: - About to write any substantive reply, an answer, an explanation, a close-out, a status.\n38: - Drafting or editing a sentence a reader will read.\n39: - About to present a recommendation, a fork, or a trade-off.\n40: - About to start a multi-step stretch of work the reader will not see inside.\n41: - About to report what a long autonomous run found.\n42: - The reader says they did not follow or asks for a plainer version.\n43: \n44: ## The rule\n45: \n46: **Write so the reader can act after one pass: the answer first, and nothing in the reply\n47: that does not carry information.**\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 1. THE REGISTER YOU ARE IN\n52: \n53: **While working: clipped.** Act rather than narrate. Open with the result, not with\n54: \"I'll now\" or \"Let me\". Batch the tool calls and report at checkpoints.\n55: \n56: **At a boundary: dense.** You are at a boundary whenever the reader is about to decide\n57: something, act on something or take the work over: a handoff, a close-out, a decision\n58: point. Verdict first, then the receipts. Reason about the problem, not about yourself.\n59: Everything else is working.\n60: \n61: **Complex topic, simple words.** When the subject is technical or layered, explain it plainly the first time, not only after the reader asks: what it is, why it matters to them, what they do next. Use a term only when the reader needs it, and define it on first use. Simpler words, same claim: never drop a caveat or a number to get there.\n62: \n63: The failure this prevents: the wrong register. Narration nobody reads, the verdict buried\n64: in working notes or the working notes inflated into a report.\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: ## 2. LENGTH\n69: \n70: **Match length to the question.** Length is earned by the reader's need, never by the work you did to get there.\n71: \n72: **Choose by reader impact before you write.** Decide who will read this and what they already hold. Keep what the reader would notice, act on or\n73: decide differently because of. Merge the items that have the same effect for them. How the\n74: work was done stays out unless it changes how far the reader can trust the result.\n75: \n76: **Concise is not compressed.** Concise cuts what the reader does not need and stops. Compressed cuts further and takes the connective tissue with it: the because, the second half of a contrast, the noun that a later \"this\" points back to. After a cut, check the joints. Every cut this file asks for answers to that floor.\n77: \n78: The failure this prevents: the answer is in there, and they did not find it, under a\n79: record of the work they never needed. Or the cut went too far, and the reader rebuilds the\n80: argument the reply no longer states.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 81]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md, lines 1-80\n1: ---\n2: title: \"Rule: Communication\"\n3: description: \"Write so the reader can act after one pass: no table in a reply, nothing that does not carry information.\"\n4: trigger_phrases:\n5:   - \"cut filler\"\n6:   - \"empty opener\"\n7:   - \"match length to the question\"\n8:   - \"no tables\"\n9:   - \"can you say that more plainly\"\n10:   - \"I don't follow\"\n11:   - \"too abstract\"\n12:   - \"number the steps\"\n13:   - \"item cap\"\n14:   - \"reply too long\"\n15:   - \"say each fact once\"\n16:   - \"one idea per sentence\"\n17:   - \"plain words\"\n18:   - \"em dash\"\n19:   - \"reads like terminal output\"\n20:   - \"concise is not compressed\"\n21:   - \"recommend one option\"\n22:   - \"buried the verdict\"\n23:   - \"say where you are going\"\n24:   - \"time estimate\"\n25: importance_tier: important\n26: contextType: reference\n27: version: 1.5.0.0\n28: ---\n29: \n30: # Rule: Communication\n31: \n32: > Routed from [`REPO RULES.md`](../../REPO%20RULES.md). Load before writing any substantive reply.\n33: > Expands `AGENTS.md`, never overrides it. Where they appear to disagree, `AGENTS.md` wins and this file is wrong. Say so.\n34: \n35: ## Fires when\n36: \n37: - About to write any substantive reply, an answer, an explanation, a close-out, a status.\n38: - Drafting or editing a sentence a reader will read.\n39: - About to present a recommendation, a fork, or a trade-off.\n40: - About to start a multi-step stretch of work the reader will not see inside.\n41: - About to report what a long autonomous run found.\n42: - The reader says they did not follow or asks for a plainer version.\n43: \n44: ## The rule\n45: \n46: **Write so the reader can act after one pass: the answer first, and nothing in the reply\n47: that does not carry information.**\n48: \n49: ---\n50: \n51: ## 1. THE REGISTER YOU ARE IN\n52: \n53: **While working: clipped.** Act rather than narrate. Open with the result, not with\n54: \"I'll now\" or \"Let me\". Batch the tool calls and report at checkpoints.\n55: \n56: **At a boundary: dense.** You are at a boundary whenever the reader is about to decide\n57: something, act on something or take the work over: a handoff, a close-out, a decision\n58: point. Verdict first, then the receipts. Reason about the problem, not about yourself.\n59: Everything else is working.\n60: \n61: **Complex topic, simple words.** When the subject is technical or layered, explain it plainly the first time, not only after the reader asks: what it is, why it matters to them, what they do next. Use a term only when the reader needs it, and define it on first use. Simpler words, same claim: never drop a caveat or a number to get there.\n62: \n63: The failure this prevents: the wrong register. Narration nobody reads, the verdict buried\n64: in working notes or the working notes inflated into a report.\n65: \n66: ---\n67: \n68: ## 2. LENGTH\n69: \n70: **Match length to the question.** Length is earned by the reader's need, never by the work you did to get there.\n71: \n72: **Choose by reader impact before you write.** Decide who will read this and what they already hold. Keep what the reader would notice, act on or\n73: decide differently because of. Merge the items that have the same effect for them. How the\n74: work was done stays out unless it changes how far the reader can trust the result.\n75: \n76: **Concise is not compressed.** Concise cuts what the reader does not need and stops. Compressed cuts further and takes the connective tissue with it: the because, the second half of a contrast, the noun that a later \"this\" points back to. After a cut, check the joints. Every cut this file asks for answers to that floor.\n77: \n78: The failure this prevents: the answer is in there, and they did not find it, under a\n79: record of the work they never needed. Or the cut went too far, and the reader rebuilds the\n80: argument the reply no longer states.\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 81]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/.skilled/repo-rules/communication.md\",\"limit\":80}"},"time":{"start":1794564820191,"end":1794564820665}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794564820854,"sessionID":"ses_e2b9b776cffe9oHJ15dLLxNWNn","part":{"partID":"prt_1d4660a6e001iObg3vwFnZwBti","sessionID":"ses_e2b9b776cffe9oHJ15dLLxNWNn","messageID":"msg_1d465f662001Y2f0VtDmQogpYH","type":"tool","id":"call_5517fdb81d7d4dfcad552661","tool":"shell","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs","workdir":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research"},"output":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs\nindex 20fc5fcb4d..3bae01bc4f 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs\n@@ -283,6 +283,44 @@ export async function briefDelivered({ runtime, locator, loadSession, codexConfi\n   return 'unknown';\n }\n \n+/**\n+ * Pick the session a DSH prompt opened among the sessions a turn added.\n+ *\n+ * A DSH turn can add helper sessions beside its own, and only the session the\n+ * prompt opened holds that prompt as its first user message, so the prompt\n+ * decides between them and a tie names none.\n+ *\n+ * @param {object} options\n+ * @param {string[]} options.before - Session ids the store held before the turn.\n+ * @param {string[]} options.after - Session ids the store held after the turn.\n+ * @param {string} options.prompt - The prompt the turn ran.\n+ * @param {(id: string) => Promise<string | null>} options.firstUserText - Reads a\n+ *   session's first user message.\n+ * @returns {Promise<string | null>} The session the prompt opened, or null.\n+ */\n+export async function promptSessionId({ before, after, prompt, firstUserText }) {\n+  if (!Array.isArray(before) || !Array.isArray(after)) return null;\n+  if (typeof prompt !== 'string' || prompt.length === 0) return null;\n+\n+  const known = new Set(before);\n+  const added = [...new Set(after)].filter((id) => !known.has(id));\n+  const wanted = prompt.trim();\n+  const matched = [];\n+\n+  for (const id of added) {\n+    let text;\n+    try {\n+      text = await firstUserText(id);\n+    } catch {\n+      continue;\n+    }\n+    if (typeof text !== 'string') continue;\n+    if (text.trim() === wanted) matched.push(id);\n+  }\n+\n+  return matched.length === 1 ? matched[0] : null;\n+}\n+\n // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n // Run-log backfill\n // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n","title":"shell","metadata":{"metadata":{"status":"completed","truncated":false,"exit":0},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"diff --git a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs\nindex 20fc5fcb4d..3bae01bc4f 100644\n--- a/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs\n+++ b/.skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs\n@@ -283,6 +283,44 @@ export async function briefDelivered({ runtime, locator, loadSession, codexConfi\n   return 'unknown';\n }\n \n+/**\n+ * Pick the session a DSH prompt opened among the sessions a turn added.\n+ *\n+ * A DSH turn can add helper sessions beside its own, and only the session the\n+ * prompt opened holds that prompt as its first user message, so the prompt\n+ * decides between them and a tie names none.\n+ *\n+ * @param {object} options\n+ * @param {string[]} options.before - Session ids the store held before the turn.\n+ * @param {string[]} options.after - Session ids the store held after the turn.\n+ * @param {string} options.prompt - The prompt the turn ran.\n+ * @param {(id: string) => Promise<string | null>} options.firstUserText - Reads a\n+ *   session's first user message.\n+ * @returns {Promise<string | null>} The session the prompt opened, or null.\n+ */\n+export async function promptSessionId({ before, after, prompt, firstUserText }) {\n+  if (!Array.isArray(before) || !Array.isArray(after)) return null;\n+  if (typeof prompt !== 'string' || prompt.length === 0) return null;\n+\n+  const known = new Set(before);\n+  const added = [...new Set(after)].filter((id) => !known.has(id));\n+  const wanted = prompt.trim();\n+  const matched = [];\n+\n+  for (const id of added) {\n+    let text;\n+    try {\n+      text = await firstUserText(id);\n+    } catch {\n+      continue;\n+    }\n+    if (typeof text !== 'string') continue;\n+    if (text.trim() === wanted) matched.push(id);\n+  }\n+\n+  return matched.length === 1 ? matched[0] : null;\n+}\n+\n // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n // Run-log backfill\n // ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"command\":\"git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime/scripts/routing-accuracy/command-offer.mjs\",\"workdir\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research\"}"},"time":{"start":1794564819566,"end":1794564820854}}}}
